  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2017-06-28T17:34:57.745Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The efficiency release for NetCode was a great idea and greatly reduced bandwidth consumption for avatars around you. Nice work on that, I'm sure that took a good long time.\n\nPlease insert some polish to this feature: It needs to be more precise when you are close to another avatar. Some players enjoy getting very close to each other and high five, touch fingers, pat heads, but when the algorithm has put the distance off by 2 or three inches, the immersion evaporates like VR water doesn't.\n\nIn short, when someone's avatar or hands are within, say, 2 feet (~2/3 meters) of you, that individual and yourself should share more detailed location information.\n\nThanks!",
